# Runtime state of a checkout deployment. The app resolves these paths against
# the config file (config.py _find_config): the repo root in a checkout, or the
# directory of a config.json that lives elsewhere (data/). The patterns are
# therefore depth-independent. config.py and updater.py write "<name>.json.tmp";
# youtube_streamer.py writes a hidden ".<name>.<random>.tmp".
config.json
update_state.json
youtube_token.json
*.chat.json
*.json.tmp
.*.tmp
cloudflared/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.tz
recordings/
chat/
*:Zone.Identifier
client_secret*.json
credentials*.json
.venv/
*.bak
# Deployment settings (docs/running.md). No .env template ships yet; the
# negation keeps a future .env.example addable without `git add -f`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
*.log
.coverage
htmlcov/
